#{[17592186570733 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570733 #edb/ref 1069 "q-152269" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570733 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570733 #edb/ref 1071 "The parabola $y={x}^{2}$ and the line $y=21-4x$ intersect at the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),$ where ${x}_{1}<{x}_{2}.$ What is the value of ${y}_{1}-{y}_{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570733 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fa4d8a0-3fad-569b-a952-bc2efe6c446d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570733 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to solve the following system consisting of the equations of the curves:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &={x}^{2} \\\\ y &=21-4x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSetting the equations equal to one another and solving, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =21-4x \\\\ {x}^{2}+4x-21 & =0 \\\\ (x+7)(x-3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-7,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}<{x}_{2},$ the $x$-coordinates of the intersection points are ${x}_{1}=-7$ and ${x}_{2}=3.$ \n\nTo find the $y$-coordinates of the intersection points, we plug these values into either curve. Let's choose the parabola since it's simpler.\n\n- Substituting ${x}_{1}=-7,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(-7)^{2} \\\\  & =49,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso one point of intersection is $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-7,49).$\n\n- Substituting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} & ={x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(3)^{2} \\\\  & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the other point of intersection is $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,9).$\n\nTherefore, ${y}_{1}=49,\\,{y}_{2}=9,$ and\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}=49-9=40.\n$$\n\nA sketch of the situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/8c/8ca9ba76d66d80a0a564fbefd02342d3f63d99f6fbd907b736cdc9acee79b174.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186570658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1069 "q-250171" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the line $y=x+3k$ does **not** intersect the parabola $y={x}^{2}+5x+k,$ find the range of possible values of $k.$\n\n$k$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "768c8258-584d-53be-9ed2-7212820baebf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570743 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine whether the line $y=x+3k$ intersects the parabola $y={x}^{2}+5x+k,$ we need to solve the following system of equations for the two curves:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &={x}^{2}+5x+k \\\\ y &=x+3k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSetting the equations equal to one another and writing in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+k & =x+3k \\\\ {x}^{2}+4x-2k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve this equation using the quadratic formula with $a=1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=-2k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{(4)^{2}-4(1)(-2k)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{16+8k}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the line and parabola do not intersect, our quadratic equation must have no real solutions; hence, the expression inside the square root must be negative. Setting up and solving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16+8k & <0 \\\\ 8k & <-16 \\\\ k & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of possible values of $k$ is $k<-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570814 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4096c219-d4f7-5387-84d1-ee267dbd82e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570814 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570838 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570838 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "800ad617-00fa-53b6-9712-0876d2b3638a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570838 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570852 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570852 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5c66e70-a6e2-575d-9123-3d8008a49c0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570852 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570868 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570868 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e5ad979e-ed88-5992-82ff-1d7fe7e01451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570868 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570705 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570876 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186570838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570876 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdd51c38-56e7-5039-8456-0a3511d2b17e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186570876 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186570728 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
